{{!-- EMAIL - WORKR 02 - Reframe (Day 2). Params: firstName, readinessLink. Subject is set by the sender, not here. --}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Applying to more jobs may not fix the problem</title>
</head>

<body style="margin:0; padding:0; background-color:#f4f7fb; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#111827;">
  <table
    role="presentation"
    cellpadding="0"
    cellspacing="0"
    border="0"
    width="100%"
    style="width:100%; margin:0; padding:0; background-color:#f4f7fb;"
  >
    <tr>
      <td align="center" style="padding:32px 16px;">

        <table
          role="presentation"
          cellpadding="0"
          cellspacing="0"
          border="0"
          width="100%"
          style="width:100%; max-width:620px; background-color:#ffffff; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:14px;"
        >
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:30px 30px 26px 30px;">

              <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-size:15px; line-height:24px; color:#111827;">
                Hi {{firstName}},
              </p>

              <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-size:15px; line-height:24px; color:#111827;">
                Suppose you applied to 100 jobs last month and received only 2 interview calls. The instinctive solution is: "Next month I'll apply to 300." But that only works if application volume was the problem.
              </p>

              <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-size:15px; line-height:24px; color:#111827;">
                Imagine instead that recruiters are rejecting your profile because your resume doesn't communicate your experience at the level you're targeting. Or you're applying to roles where your experience doesn't match the hiring team's requirement. Or you're relying entirely on job portals while candidates entering through referrals and recruiter outreach are getting reviewed first.
              </p>

              <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-size:15px; line-height:24px; color:#111827;">
                Then increasing application volume doesn't fix anything. It simply increases the number of times the same broken process gets repeated.
              </p>

              <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-size:15px; line-height:24px; color:#111827;">
                That's why the first question shouldn't be "How many jobs should I apply to?" It should be "Where exactly is my interview pipeline breaking?"
              </p>

              <p style="margin:0 0 24px 0; font-size:15px; line-height:24px; color:#111827;">
                We've created a diagnostic around that question:
                <a
                  href="{{readinessLink}}"
                  target="_blank"
                  style="color:#2563eb; font-weight:700; text-decoration:underline;"
                >Check your Product Company Readiness &rarr;</a>
              </p>

              <p style="margin:0; font-size:15px; line-height:24px; color:#111827;">
                &mdash; Sunyul<br />
                InterviewCall
              </p>

            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>

        <table
          role="presentation"
          cellpadding="0"
          cellspacing="0"
          border="0"
          width="100%"
          style="width:100%; max-width:620px;"
        >
          <tr>
            <td align="center" style="padding:16px 8px 0 8px;">
              <p style="margin:0; font-size:12px; line-height:18px; color:#64748b;">
                You are receiving this because you signed up on WorkR. If you would rather not hear from us, just reply to this email and let us know.
              </p>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>

      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</body>
</html>
